Package: indi-scopelink
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: INDI driver for the Astrolabs ScopeLink telescope controller
 ScopeLink drives a focuser, a rotator, a telescope front flap, a flat panel,
 two mirror fans and, depending on the hardware generation, two auxiliary
 power outputs and a powered USB hub, all over one USB connection.
 .
 The driver publishes the controller as a single INDI device carrying the
 focuser, rotator, dust cap and light box interfaces, so that any INDI client
 such as KStars can run autofocus, rotate the field, open and close the flap
 and take flat frames. Which motor does which job is the controller's own
 setting, and the driver offers a device only where a motor is assigned to it
 and calibrated for it.
 .
 The controller's configuration, fault store and motor calibration are readable
 and writable from the driver, and its firmware can be replaced over the same
 serial port, which needs no DFU mode and no privileges beyond access to the
 port itself.
 .
 A simulation mode and a pseudo terminal simulator are included, so the driver
 can be tried without a controller attached.
